Causal Inference What If by Hernan and Robins (@inquiry-source-causal: 0, is #reference) { r_00C7EB9DE7F8A7314754A058EE
Miguel A. Hernán and James M. Robins, **Causal Inference: What If**. The authors' suggested bibliographic citation is 2020, Boca Raton: Chapman & Hall/CRC. This Record's inspected online revision is dated **19 August 2026**, not the January 2025 PDF still returned by some searches. [Author book page](https://miguelhernan.org/whatifbook) · [Dated author PDF](https://miguelhernan.org/s/hernanrobins_WhatIf_19aug26.pdf).

The author page provides free download and warns that revisions may occur without a change log. The inspected PDF has 365 pages and a 2020/2026 copyright notice reserving rights. Free access is not an open redistribution licence. Keep the book, source images, datasets and companion implementations external; link the authorized copy and retain attribution. No book text or author code is incorporated into the original programs.

**Selected inspection — 1 November 2026:** read the title, copyright and contents, then selected actual text in sections 2.2–2.4 (printed pages 17–22), 3.1 (27–28), 3.3–3.4 (32–35) and 8.4 (115–116). Table 2.2 on printed page 17 was also visually inspected. The common block reconstructs only its bounded standardization/weighting calculation from aggregated numerical counts. The text treats the named entries as representatives of large population groups; do not interpret its absence-of-random-variability account as a general theorem about imbalance in a twenty-person sample. No real participant data analysis, intervention or clinical advice is claimed.

**Progressive reading:** chapters 1–3 establish the intervention and identification vocabulary; work their reasoning alongside the existing finite probability and randomized-comparison lessons. Then read chapter 4 for target-dependent comparisons, chapters 6–8 for graphs, confounding and selection, and chapter 9 for measurement bias. These broader chapters, exercises and companion programs are assignments, not a claim of complete inspection. Later modelling and longitudinal parts belong to advanced inquiry/statistics after their mathematical preparation. The common service examples, complete-law counterexamples, programs and independent checks are original teaching material.

**Return:** [Scientific inquiry and practice](../Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB).
